      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To investigate the single nucleotide polymorphism 4 (SNP4) of the apolipoprotein A5 (APOA5) gene possible association with coronary heart disease(CHD) and its distribution of in Chinese Han population."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "APOA5 SNP4 genotyping was performed using polymerase chain reaction and Hae III restriction fragment length polymorphism analysis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "APOA5 allelic frequencies of T, C were 0.435, 0.565 and 0.374, 0.626 in CHD group and control group, respectively. There is significant difference in allele and genotype frequencies between CHD group and control group (P<0.05). The levels of plasma high density lipoprotein in CHD patients with CC genotype were higher than those in CHD patients with other genotypes (P<0.01). The frequencies of T allele and C allele in Chinese was significantly different from those in Caucasians (0.374 vs 0.663, 0.626 vs 0.337, P<0.01). The C allele was much more common in Chinese population."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The association is found between the Hae III polymorphism and CHD, There is a significant correlation between the CC genotype of the APOA5 and the levels of plasma high density lipoprotein-cholosteal in the CHD group."
        }
      ]},
